"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}], "questions": [{"responses": [{"id": 0, "correct": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0}, {"id": 1, "correct": 1, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}]}], "stimuli_ids": [], "id": 10, "template_override": 1}, {"type": "DWS", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " \nWatch <span class=\"italic\">Due Date</span> and create a timeline.\n", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Take Away", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Listening", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self Assessment.", "type": "text"}]}], "questions": [{"responses": [{"id": 0, "correct": 1, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "engenn9le04ob09re7pdf01.pdf", "type": "pdf"}]}]}], "stimuli_ids": [], "id": 11, "template_override": 1}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "stimuli": [{"id": 0, "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}]}, {"_data": [], "type": "audio", "title": "", "template_override": 1, "id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"text": "", "image": "engenn9le04ob09re2img05.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: So, how is your week going?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I'm telling you, it's really not my week. I should have stayed in bed all week.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: You told me that things were a bit difficult at work. What else happened?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I took the bus downtown today. It should have been a smooth trip. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: But ...", "image": "engenn9le04ob09re2img05.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: This young guy got on the bus and sat in the last empty seat. At the next stop, an elderly woman got on the bus. The young guy could have offered his seat but he didn't.  I asked the young guy if he would get up. He told me he was tired!  I was incensed! I thought he was being so selfish.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: So then what happened?", "image": "engenn9le04ob09re2img01.jpg", "time": "16500", "id": 2}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I went up the the driver and told him that this guy refused to give up his seat. The driver stopped the bus and went and told this guy that he had to vacate the seat for this elderly woman. The guy got up and it was then that I noticed he had a cast on his ankle! I wouldn't have told him to move if I had seen the cast! I should have minded my own business! I felt awful and was so embarrassed!<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Well, you should have been more observant and aware of his emotional state, but you thought you were doing the right thing. Don't beat yourself up about it. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I guess I have to keep working on my emotional intelligence!", "image": "engenn9le04ob09re2img05.jpg", "time": "36000", "id": 3}], "coverimg": "engenn9le04ob09re2img05.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn9le04ob09re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}]}], "type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "An Emotional Week", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Let It Go", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 9, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 4, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe hypothetical situations in spoken interactions according to work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le04ob09re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Talking Hypothetically About the Past", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">could have</span>, <span class=\"italic\">should have</span> and <span class=\"italic\">would have</span> to talk about things that were possible in the past and may or may not have happened. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The structure: <br/><br/><span class=\"strong\"> Subject    + modal verb    + have     + verb (past participle)</span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">I             could              have        done<br/> You             should              have        made<br/> She            would               have        said</span><br/><br/>  You use <span class=\"italic\">could have</span> to talk about possibilities if something had been different in the past.<br/> For example: <span class=\"italic\">The young guy could have offered her his seat but he didn't.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">should have</span> to talk about past events that did not happen and to speculate about events that may or may not have happened.<br/> For example: <span class=\"italic\"> I should have stayed in bed all week.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">should not have</span> to speculate negatively about what may or may not have happened.<br/> You also use <span class=\"italic\">should not have</span> to express regret for past actions.<br/><br/>  You use <span class=\"italic\">would have</span> to imagine a result if something had been different in the past.<br/> For example: <span class=\"italic\">I wouldn't have told him to move if I had seen the cast!", "type": "text"}, {"content": "* <span class=\"italic\">Would have</span> expresses more certainty about the result than <span class=\"italic\">could have</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I should have stayed in bed all week.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It should have been a smooth trip. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The young guy could have offered her his seat but he didn't.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I wouldn't have told him to move if I had seen the cast! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I should have minded my own business!", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Reported Speech and Questions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use reported speech when you are saying (reporting) what other people said. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you tell people what someone has said in the past, you generally make the verb tense 'more in the past'. You need to change the verb to the next past form. <br/><br/>For example: <br/><br/>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Direct Speech\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Reported Speech\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">like</span> him.\\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He said he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">liked</span> him.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"I'<span class=\\\"strong\\\">m coming</span> to the party.\\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He said he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">was coming.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"I already <span class=\\\"strong\\\">ate</span>.\\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He said he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">had</span> already <span class=\\\"strong\\\">eaten</span>.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">can</span> cook.\\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He told me he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">could</span> cook.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"Where do you <span class=\\\"strong\\\">live</span>?\\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He asked me where I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">lived</span>.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "You have to change the pronoun if you are reporting what someone else said. Compare these two sentences. In each case the person actually said \"I don't want to go.\"", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul><li>I said, \u201cI don't want to go.\u201d  >  I said <span class=\"strong\">I</span> didn't want to go.</li> <li>Bill said, \u201cI don't want to go.\u201d  >  Bill said <span class=\"strong\">he</span> didn't want to go.</li></ul>Look at the chart below to see the changes in verb tense.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":10,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Direct Speech\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Reported Speech\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Simple Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Simple Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Progressive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Progressive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Simple Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Perect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Progressive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Perfect Progressive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Future Simple (will)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Conditional (would)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal <span class=\\\"italic\\\">can</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal <span class=\\\"italic\\\">could</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal <span class=\\\"italic\\\">may\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal <span class=\\\"italic\\\">might\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "You told me that things were a bit difficult at work.", "type": "example"}, {"content": " I asked the young guy if he would get up.", "type": "example"}, {"content": " He told me he was tired!  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": " I told him that this guy refused to give up his seat.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "He told this guy he had to vacate the seat for the elderly woman.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "elderly", "type": "name"}, {"content": "old, like a senior citizen", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: At the next stop, an elderly woman got on the bus.   ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le04ob09aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about reactions and behavior in different situations.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to offer", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to give someone the opportunity to accept or take something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The young guy could have offered her his seat but he didn't.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le04ob09aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "smooth", "type": "name"}, {"content": "happening or done without any problems", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It should have been a smooth trip. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le04ob09aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to refuse", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to say that you will not accept something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I went up the the driver and told him that this guy refused to give up his seat.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le04ob09aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "incensed", "type": "name"}, {"content": "very angry", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I was incensed by his rude behavior.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le04ob09aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to vacate ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to leave a job or position", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The driver stopped the bus and went and told this guy he had to vacate the seat for the elderly woman. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le04ob09aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "cast", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a hard covering that is put on an arm or leg so that a broken bone can heal", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The guy got up and it was then that I noticed he had a cast on his ankle!  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le04ob09aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "embarrassed", "type": "name"}, {"content": "feeling confused or foolish in front of people", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I felt awful and was so embarrassed!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le04ob09aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "observant", "type": "name"}, {"content": "good at watching and listening", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You should have been more observant and aware of his emotional state.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le04ob09aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Watch the 2010 movie <span class=\"italic\">Due Date</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make notes about all the things that happen to Peter.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Create a timeline to summarize Peter's experience.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about reactions and behavior.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about hypothetical situations about the past.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use reported speech.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I watch a movie and create a timeline.", "type": "text"}]}]}